locked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Hi,\n\nfrom my own tests the events exposed via `ControllingEvents` no longer seem to work on Fabric, starting from around Minecraft 26.1.\n\n`com.blamejared.controlling.platform.FabricPlatformHelper` guards all actual event triggers with `FabricLoader.getInstance().isModLoaded(\"fabric\")`.\n\nI guess in earlier versions Fabric had a hardcoded legacy compatibility for the mod id `fabric` (probably delegating to `fabric-api` or `fabric-api-base`), since that hasn't been officially in use anymore since quite some time.\nAround Minecraft 26.1 this compat seems to have been removed and the check for mod id `fabric` now always yields false, effectively rendering Controlling's events on Fabric useless.\n\nI assume the check in `FabricPlatformHelper` is supposed to check for the presence of the Fabric Event API, so that no class loader problems occur when Fabric API is not installed.\nIf that is the case, the checks should be changed to `fabric-api-base` since that is the current module that houses the Event API.\n\nIdeally, you could release this fix for 26.1 and 26.2 alongside 26.3.\n\nThanks in advance :‌)","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jaredlll08/Controlling/issues/240/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jaredlll08/Controlling/issues/240/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jaredlll08/Controlling/issues/237","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jaredlll08/Controlling","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jaredlll08/Controlling/issues/237/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jaredlll08/Controlling/issues/237/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jaredlll08/Controlling/issues/237/events","html_url":"https://github.com/jaredlll08/C